# Build artifacts
/target/
**/target/

# Cargo.lock: tracked for binary crates / workspaces; ignored for libraries.
# SupaZip ships binaries (supazip-gui, supazip-cli), so Cargo.lock is committed.

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local environment files (never commit secrets)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs
*.log

# rust-analyzer
rust-project.json

# Vendored reference project (PeaZip) is a nested clone; never index.
# The PeaZip sources exist for design inspiration only and are not part of
# the SupaZip build. Remove this exclusion if you ever decide to vendor
# PeaZip sources into the SupaZip tree as a non-nested-repo.
# (PeaZip's own .git is the source of truth for those files.)
# Nothing to add here — `PeaZip/` is a separate checkout, not a subdir of
# this repo's tree. If a `PeaZip/.git` is ever moved into the tree, exclude
# its metadata with `/PeaZip/.git/`.
